Generated by Stinger-IPC code generator {{generator.version}}.

Integration test server for the {{stinger.name}} interface.

Unlike server_demo.py, this is not meant to run forever or be watched by a
human: it emits every signal on a short interval, validates every method
call/command/property update it receives against the value
client_integration_test.py is expected to send, and prints one
``[CHECK] <name> ... PASS|FAIL`` line per thing it validates, then a final
``RESULT: PASS|FAIL (n/m checks)`` line and exits - 0 if every check passed,
1 otherwise. It stops on its own once every expected check has come in, or
after MAX_LIFETIME_SECONDS, whichever is first, so it never has to be killed
by hand.

Start this first, then run client_integration_test.py (same MQTT_HOSTNAME/
MQTT_PORT) in another process.
